+#### [b8] bcopy *dst_addr* <sub>[REG:ADDR]</sub> *src_addr* <sub>[REG:SAME_AS_PREV]</sub> *width* <sub>[REG/CONST:OFFSET]</sub>
+Copy bytes: `RAM[dst + i] := RAM[src + i]`
+
+               A non-negative length copies that many bytes upward starting
+               at the given addresses, one byte at a time.
+               A negative length copies downward starting with the byte
+               just below the given addresses.
+               The sign is taken from the value even when it is in a register.
+
+#### [ba] bzero *dst_addr* <sub>[REG:ADDR]</sub> *width* <sub>[REG/CONST:OFFSET]</sub>
+Zero bytes: `RAM[dst + i] := 0`
+
+               The length works like the one of `bcopy`.
+
